AHS-005 — Layered Architecture

Document ID: AHS-005
Title: Layered Architecture
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

Architectural Views: Logical, Conceptual

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical layered architecture of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

The layered architecture partitions the system into cohesive architectural layers, each with clearly defined responsibilities, interfaces, and dependencies. It establishes the structural organization that governs engineering cognition while preserving modularity, maintainability, and scalability.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Canonical architectural layers
Layer responsibilities
Layer interfaces
Layer dependencies
Layer interaction rules
Layer isolation principles

It does not define implementation technologies or deployment topologies.

3. Layering Principles

The Atlas layered architecture SHALL adhere to the following principles:

Each layer has a single architectural responsibility.
Layers communicate only through defined interfaces.
Layers SHALL NOT directly manipulate the internal state of other layers.
Dependencies SHALL flow downward through the architecture unless explicitly permitted.
Cross-cutting governance applies uniformly to all layers.
